  <!-- ============================================================
       01 — CROSSFIRE LEGENDS
       ============================================================ -->

  <section
    id="crossfire-legends"
    class="project-feature"
  >
    <div class="site-shell">

      <div class="project-heading-row">

        <span class="project-index">
          01 / CURRENT
        </span>

        <h2 class="project-title">
          CrossFire<br />
          Legends
        </h2>

        <span class="project-date">
          2025 — NOW
        </span>

      </div>


      <p class="project-subtitle">
        Helping build and operate the Indonesian community
        <span class="marker">
          from the beginning.
        </span>
      </p>


      <!-- Main CFL image -->

      <figure class="pasted-photo rotate-right">

        <span class="photo-tape top-center"></span>

        <img
          src="/images/cflc.jpg"
          alt="CrossFire Legends community and esports activities"
          loading="lazy"
        />

        <figcaption class="photo-caption">
          Indonesia + SEA ↗
        </figcaption>

      </figure>


      <!-- ======================================================
           CONTEXT
           ====================================================== -->

      <div class="project-details">

        <div class="project-description">

          <p>
            I joined CrossFire Legends while the Indonesian community
            was still being built. Today, I handle much of its
            day-to-day operation — from player communication and
            recurring activities to creators, feedback, and tournaments.
          </p>

          <p>
            The work changes depending on what the community needs.
            Some days that means answering players and preparing
            announcements. Others involve running an activity,
            coordinating creators, supporting tournament participants,
            or collecting issues that need to go back to the team.
          </p>

          <p>
            I also support community-facing esports work across
            Southeast Asia, particularly around tournament communication
            and coordination.
          </p>

        </div>


        <dl class="project-facts">

          <div class="project-fact">
            <dt>Role</dt>
            <dd>Community Manager</dd>
          </div>

          <div class="project-fact">
            <dt>Primary Market</dt>
            <dd>Indonesia</dd>
          </div>

          <div class="project-fact">
            <dt>Regional Work</dt>
            <dd>Southeast Asia</dd>
          </div>

          <div class="project-fact">
            <dt>Community</dt>
            <dd>Discord · Facebook · WhatsApp</dd>
          </div>

          <div class="project-fact">
            <dt>Areas</dt>
            <dd>Community · Creators · Esports</dd>
          </div>

        </dl>

      </div>


      <!-- ======================================================
           WHAT I HANDLE
           ====================================================== -->

      <div class="tournament-note">

        <p class="handwritten note note-large note-left">
          what the day-to-day actually looks like ↓
        </p>


        <h3 class="tournament-note-heading">
          From launch to something<br />
          happening almost every week.
        </h3>


        <p>
          Regular community communication sits alongside quizzes,
          simple community events, mini tournaments, scrimmages,
          creator activities, and larger competitive programs.
        </p>


        <div class="project-capabilities">

          <!-- 01 -->

          <div class="capability">

            <span class="capability-number">
              01
            </span>

            <div>

              <h3>
                Community Operations
              </h3>

              <p>
                Day-to-day player communication, moderation,
                announcements, questions, onboarding, and engagement
                across the community's main channels.
              </p>

            </div>

          </div>


          <!-- 02 -->

          <div class="capability">

            <span class="capability-number">
              02
            </span>

            <div>

              <h3>
                Weekly Activities
              </h3>

              <p>
                Recurring quizzes, comment-based events, mini
                tournaments, fast scrimmages, and other activities
                that give players something to join.
              </p>

            </div>

          </div>


          <!-- 03 -->

          <div class="capability">

            <span class="capability-number">
              03
            </span>

            <div>

              <h3>
                Creator Programs
              </h3>

              <p>
                Communicate program information, recap creator work
                and submissions, track completion, and contact
                creators who qualify for rewards.
              </p>

            </div>

          </div>


          <!-- 04 -->

          <div class="capability">

            <span class="capability-number">
              04
            </span>

            <div>

              <h3>
                Player Feedback
              </h3>

              <p>
                Track recurring questions, gameplay issues, bugs,
                complaints, and requests from players and bring
                useful feedback back to the team.
              </p>

            </div>

          </div>


          <!-- 05 -->

          <div class="capability">

            <span class="capability-number">
              05
            </span>

            <div>

              <h3>
                Tournament Operations
              </h3>

              <p>
                Support community-facing tournaments through
                participant coordination, promotion, tournament
                information, and match-day communication.
              </p>

            </div>

          </div>


          <!-- 06 -->

          <div class="capability">

            <span class="capability-number">
              06
            </span>

            <div>

              <h3>
                Player Communication
              </h3>

              <p>
                Turn game updates, campaigns, event information,
                and tournament requirements into communication
                players can understand and act on.
              </p>

            </div>

          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- ============================================================
       02 — ROAD TO ALL-STAR
       ============================================================ -->

  <section
    id="road-to-all-star"
    class="project-feature"
  >
    <div class="site-shell">

      <div class="project-heading-row">

        <span class="project-index">
          02 / PROJECT
        </span>

        <h2 class="project-title">
          Road to<br />
          All-Star
        </h2>

        <span class="project-date">
          2026
        </span>

      </div>


      <p class="project-subtitle">
        Four seasons. Four chances to qualify.
        <span class="marker marker-double">
          One All-Star.
        </span>
      </p>


      <!-- ======================================================
           PROJECT STORY
           ====================================================== -->

      <div class="project-details">

        <div class="project-description">

          <p>
            Clash for Glory: Road to All-Star is a community
            tournament series I'm working on for CrossFire Legends
            Indonesia.
          </p>

          <p>
            One tournament would give teams one chance to qualify.
            Road to All-Star gives them four.
          </p>

          <p>
            The series runs across four seasons, with teams competing
            for 10 places in the December All-Star. That also gives
            the community a competitive storyline that continues
            across several months instead of ending after one event.
          </p>

        </div>


        <dl class="project-facts">

          <div class="project-fact">
            <dt>Format</dt>
            <dd>4-season series</dd>
          </div>

          <div class="project-fact">
            <dt>Qualification</dt>
            <dd>4 opportunities</dd>
          </div>

          <div class="project-fact">
            <dt>Destination</dt>
            <dd>All-Star</dd>
          </div>

          <div class="project-fact">
            <dt>Final Field</dt>
            <dd>10 teams</dd>
          </div>

          <div class="project-fact">
            <dt>All-Star</dt>
            <dd>December 2026</dd>
          </div>

        </dl>

      </div>


      <!-- ======================================================
           TIMELINE
           ====================================================== -->

      <div class="tournament-timeline">

        <!-- Season 1 -->

        <div class="timeline-step current">

          <span class="timeline-current-note">
            we are here ↓
          </span>

          <span class="timeline-label">
            01
          </span>

          <span class="timeline-name">
            Season 1 · Current
          </span>

        </div>


        <!-- Season 2 -->

        <div class="timeline-step">

          <span class="timeline-label">
            02
          </span>

          <span class="timeline-name">
            Season 2 · This Month
          </span>

        </div>


        <!-- Season 3 -->

        <div class="timeline-step">

          <span class="timeline-label">
            03
          </span>

          <span class="timeline-name">
